abstract: >
  plasmonX is an open-source computational platform for simulating the nanoplasmonic response of complex nanostructures using atomistic approaches, such as fluctuating charge (ωFQ) and fluctuating charge and dipole (ωFQFμ), and implicit models, such as the boundary element method (BEM), with Python interfaces for input and post-processing. This file provides citation metadata for users.

keywords:
  - nanoplasmonics
  - ωFQ
  - ωFQFμ
  - BEM

